# Line endings.
#
# Since GeoDMS 20.18.0 every text blob in this repository is stored with LF.
# `* text=auto` makes git normalise on commit and convert back on checkout, so a
# Windows working tree still gets CRLF while the history stays on one convention.
#
# Before this, the repository was split roughly in half -- 696 CRLF blobs against
# 629 LF blobs -- and 45 files had drifted into a mix of both. That mix could not
# heal by itself: git skips normalisation for any file whose index version already
# contains CR, so every bare LF written into a CRLF file was committed verbatim and
# stayed there. With all blobs on LF that exception no longer applies, and `git add`
# normalises every working copy again, mixed ones included.
#
# One-time repair for a working tree cloned before this change: batch\NormalizeCRLF.bat
* text=auto

# Windows-only scripts. cmd.exe itself runs LF batch files fine (verified on
# Windows 11 26200 against goto / call :label / for /f / if-else / ^-continuation),
# but pinning CRLF costs nothing and keeps older Windows versions out of trouble.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Visual Studio rewrites these with CRLF the moment you add a file or change a
# property in the IDE. Pinning CRLF keeps that from showing up as a diff.
*.sln     text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj text eol=crlf
*.filters text eol=crlf
*.pyproj  text eol=crlf

# vcpkg hashes its triplet files into the ABI of every package built with them,
# so a checkout that rewrites their line endings invalidates the binary cache and
# rebuilds every port from source. Pin them the way vcpkg wrote them.
vcpkg-triplets/*.cmake text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts MUST stay LF: bash (the WSL Linux build via nsi/CreateLinuxSetup.sh
# and the Linux unit-test launchers TestLinux*Unit.sh / RunLinuxGUITests.sh) fails on
# CRLF ($'\r': command not found). Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to
# CRLF on checkout/merge and breaks the Linux build + unit tests.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never eligible for eol conversion. Git's own detection already
# classifies these; the rules below just make it explicit and unconditional.
*.bmp  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.cur  binary
*.ttf  binary

# UTF-16LE, so it looks binary to git and must stay that way. Its sibling
# shv/dll/res/DmShv32.rc is plain text and is covered by `* text=auto` above.
qtgui/exe/GeoDmsGuiQt.rc binary
